frag_traces, and the case where span*inv rounds such that a real bucket index exceeds 65535. Is
+/-2 actually sufficient, and is the clamp in bucketOf safe on BOTH ends? Also: does the extra
2 bytes/fragment of `q` cost more memory than the scan saves, and is the build loop O(n) as claimed?

